  "notes": [
    "K1Q:<code>:<container>. <code> is exactly 32 characters of 0123456789ABCDEFGHJKMNPQRSTVWXYZ (upper case, no separators, no I/L/O/U leniency); <container> is a K1:1 container verbatim.",
    "container key = BLAKE2b-256(\"tg-e1-transfer-v1\" || base32decode(code)); XChaCha20-Poly1305, AAD \"K1:1\"; byte arrays in the JSON are {\"$b\": base64url-no-pad}.",
    "plaintext_json is the exact byte string that was encrypted. A client that serialises differently will not reproduce k1q byte-for-byte, but MUST decode it to expect.",
    "Surrounding whitespace is trimmed before parsing. Errors: malformed (syntax), undecryptable (wrong code / tampered), wrongScope (scope != \"chat\"). All three show SecutgQuickShareBadQr.",
    "Capacity: the K1Q text must be <= 2331 bytes (QR byte mode, EC level M, version 40). Too long: keep the current master and drop history masters oldest first; if the current one alone does not fit, refuse (SecutgQuickShareTooLarge)."
  ],
